PRV-01|private input|Street address and parcel number|Subject property|Current||text|private|LAC_ASSESSOR|Withheld by design. Needed for every parcel lookup (assessed value, zoning, flood, fire and seismic zones). Never published
PRV-02|private input|Exact lease expiry date|Subject property|Current||date|private|SEC_JACK_10K25|Known only as "2030 to 2035". Read it from the lease and all amendments. The model reports every year in that range
PRV-03|private input|Current annual rent|Subject property|Current||USD|private|SEC_JACK_10K25|Read from the lease or rent roll. The model is scaled to 100 so that the owner can multiply by the real figure
PRV-04|private input|Rent increases written into the lease|Subject property|Current||percent|private|SEC_JACK_10K25|The tenant's annual report says its leases generally carry cost-of-living adjustments (TEN-27); this lease's own schedule is not known
PRV-05|private input|Renewal options: number, length, notice window and how option rent is set|Subject property|Current||text|private|SEC_JACK_10K25|Decides whether the tenant can stay without negotiating and whether rent can reset to market
PRV-06|private input|Who signed the lease and who guarantees it (the company or a franchisee)|Subject property|Current||text|private|SEC_JACK_10K25|The company is the lessee at 1,585 sites and franchisees control 387 (TEN-23, TEN-24). The credit behind this lease depends on which group it is in
PRV-07|private input|Sales of this restaurant|Subject property|Latest year||USD|private|SEC_JACK_10K25|Ask for sales reports if the lease allows it. System average is 1,874,000 a year (TEN-13); rent above about 8% of sales is heavier than the system average (TEN-33)
PRV-08|private input|Who pays for roof, structure, parking, taxes and insurance, and whether a tax reassessment after a sale passes to the tenant|Subject property|Current||text|private|BOE_P13|A sale triggers reassessment to market value (TAX-20). Whether the tenant absorbs the higher bill affects what a buyer will pay
PRV-09|private input|Owner's tax basis and depreciation already taken|Owner|Current||USD|private|IRS_409|Sets the taxable gain. Without it no after-tax figure can be stated
PRV-10|private input|How title is held (individual, trust, company) and the estate plan|Owner|Current||text|private|IRS_P551|Inherited property generally takes a new basis at the value on the date of death (TAX-26, TAX-27), which changes the case for selling during life
PRV-11|private input|Mortgage on the property: balance, rate, maturity, prepayment terms|Owner|Current||USD|private|FED_FOMC|Debt changes both risk and the cash left after a sale
PRV-12|private input|Insurance in force: who buys it, earthquake cover, deductibles, premium|Subject property|Current||text|private|USGS_UCERF3|Regional earthquake likelihood is high (HAZ-01). Whether the building is covered is in the policy, not in any public record
PRV-13|private input|Owner's other assets, income needs and capacity to carry a vacant building|Owner|Current||text|private|UST_CURVE|Decides how much single-property risk is tolerable. Not collected and never published
PRV-14|private input|Land area, building size, zoning and drive-through approval|Subject property|Current||text|private|LA_ZIMAS|Sets the value of the land if the tenant leaves. Look up in the city zoning system once the address is used privately
UNV-01|unverified|Market cap rate for this property as it stands today|Subject property|2026||percent|unverified|SEC_FCPT|No official source prices a single central Los Angeles restaurant property. Public filings give portfolio averages of 6.6% to 7.8% (CAP-12). Obtain a broker opinion of value or an appraisal
UNV-02|unverified|How much the cap rate rises as the remaining lease term shortens|United States|2026||basis points per year|unverified|SEC_NNN|No official series was found. The model uses a labelled assumption and shows the result with half and double that value
UNV-03|unverified|Population, income and traffic within one to three miles of the site|Subject trade area|Latest||various|unverified|CENSUS_QF|Needs the address, which is withheld. The Census data service also required an access key this session. City and county figures are used as context only
UNV-04|unverified|Population projection for the City of Los Angeles or any smaller area to 2035|City of Los Angeles|2026 to 2035||persons|unverified|DOF_P2A|The state publishes projections by county, not by city. The regional agency's city tables could not be opened by the page reader
UNV-05|unverified|Regional planning forecast for Los Angeles County (population, households, jobs)|Los Angeles County|2030 to 2050||persons|unverified|SCAG_2024|The county tables lie beyond the pages the reader could parse. Another workbook in this repository publishes these figures; this session could not re-read them
UNV-06|unverified|Fire hazard severity zone of the parcel|Subject property|2026||zone|unverified|OSFM_FHSZ|Needs the address. The 2025 fires burned at the wildland edge (HAZ-13); whether this parcel sits in a mapped zone is not known
UNV-07|unverified|Flood zone of the parcel|Subject property|Effective map||zone|unverified|FEMA_MSC|Needs the address
UNV-08|unverified|Liquefaction, landslide and fault-rupture zoning of the parcel|Subject property|Current||zone|unverified|CGS_SHZ|Needs the address. A seller must disclose a mapped zone to buyers (HAZ-16)
UNV-09|unverified|FEMA National Risk Index score|Los Angeles County|Latest||score|unverified|FEMA_NRI|The county report viewer returned a server error on November 10, 2026
UNV-10|unverified|Jack in the Box net loss for the full fiscal year 2025|Jack in the Box Inc. consolidated|Fiscal 2025||USD|unverified|SEC_JACK_10K25|Other workbooks in this repository state a figure. This session read the 40-week comparison only (TEN-39), so the full-year figure is left blank
UNV-11|unverified|Any California surcharge on very high incomes above the 12.3% top bracket|California|Tax year 2025||percent|unverified|FTB_RATES|The rate schedule read this session stops at 12.3%. A surcharge was not confirmed on an official page, so TAX-22 excludes it
UNV-12|unverified|Brokerage, escrow and title cost of a sale|Los Angeles|2026||percent of price|unverified|LAC_DTT|No official source. Transfer taxes are verified (TAX-17); the model adds a labelled assumption for the rest
UNV-13|unverified|Likelihood that the tenant renews this particular lease|Subject property|2030 to 2035||percent|unverified|SEC_JACK_10K25|No official source can give it. Public base rates: 76.2% of expiring net leases renewed with the same tenant (LSE-01); the tenant closed 3.9% of its restaurants in fiscal 2025 (TEN-16)
UNV-14|unverified|Whether a new drive-through could be approved at this site if the tenant leaves|Subject property|Current||text|unverified|LA_ZIMAS|Needs the address and a zoning review
UNV-15|unverified|Assessed value and current property tax bill|Subject property|2026||USD|unverified|LAC_ASSESSOR|Needs the address or parcel number
UNV-16|unverified|Crime rate around the site|Subject trade area|2026||rate|unverified|LAPD_CRIME|The legacy city dataset is frozen (SOC-10) and the replacement was not read this session; a rate also needs the address
UNV-17|unverified|Graduation rate and test results for Los Angeles Unified, and the schools serving the address|Los Angeles Unified School District|2024-25||percent|unverified|CDE_LAUSD|Only enrolment was read this session (EDU-05 to EDU-10). Assigned schools need the address
UNV-18|unverified|Insurance market conditions and the state insurer of last resort|California|2026||text|unverified|USGS_UCERF3|The state insurance regulator's page linked from an earlier workbook returned "Document Not Found" on November 10, 2026; no replacement was read
UNV-19|unverified|Environmental records for the site (underground tanks, cleanup cases)|Subject property|Current||text|unverified|LAC_ASSESSOR|The state cleanup-site database could not be opened by the page reader and needs the address
